    {
      "segment_id": "967d86495aba9acf6346a0a2",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "19",
      "locator": "paragraph 19",
      "text": "2020 Primary Voters Guide: Shannon Reid believes Douglas County leaders need to listen better to constituents",
      "sha256": "a9367d8393a7037cfd7a0a14a6848093566be24a0f1b3c8a375257f0ef322daa"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "f0d2913d7c69c2fb1e3241ab",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "20",
      "locator": "paragraph 20",
      "text": "County Government",
      "sha256": "6643ee5f05f7f83aa37ad58fc94552b6ee6636f88e894125eb9d76f43c051c92"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "c4246323f82151a40dfd2134",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "21",
      "locator": "paragraph 21",
      "text": "Jul 19, 2020 - 12:00am",
      "sha256": "d7b1e90d711f775dca1b7f38a22f4b08ab59f1c86b6d67a6c6849d755a4af1fb"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "0a59bd434ee2fd6f86efdfcb",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "22",
      "locator": "paragraph 22",
      "text": "Dylan Lysen",
      "sha256": "8152fb4179fb6b58d3ac65bb81eff9d9aaeab92794d2e9dfbc28e969488eea6c"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "4b1764a6d837d9ebdf9ad1aa",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "23",
      "locator": "paragraph 23",
      "text": "dlysen@ljworld.com",
      "sha256": "6c647cc8bd06b339f1cb17ae491376c6f6e1ccd9f06b4669777fd9b5556793c7"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "8ed9c69db0220e4d59972977",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "24",
      "locator": "paragraph 24",
      "text": "photo by: Contributed photo",
      "sha256": "c894280d9df783de8910e266e039956bd3da3d52d340b87a816f9ac532811aa6"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "8230c7943cee2495acf0f457",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "25",
      "locator": "paragraph 25",
      "text": "Shannon Reid",
      "sha256": "753038bcd2c2da932d10345b9ded4ddd97c4842c5dee5e9427dab6eef63f5f64"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "63a4186fd48d71364c38cc5e",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "26",
      "locator": "paragraph 26",
      "text": "The Douglas County Commission’s decision earlier this year to approve a $29.6 million expansion of its jail after voters rejected such a project in 2018 left Shannon Reid feeling the county leaders were not listening to their constituents.",
      "sha256": "a004523b58ce405806583feda6c5af5f36071ee75510002a8cfc6ec460497ba1"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "09ebec490d468d786e653d25",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "27",
      "locator": "paragraph 27",
      "text": "Reid, 35, said she chose to run for the County Commission to make sure community members’ voices are represented. Reid is one of three Democratic candidates running for the County Commission’s 2nd District seat.",
      "sha256": "cc758bb31a83ac88f5b2834f37d0e02ad7a4153c83e43c50caa42962f1a89996"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "df43a2a2fbf54c9444e6e16d",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "28",
      "locator": "paragraph 28",
      "text": "“I’ve been feeling disheartened with the county’s leadership in remaining stuck in that project despite voters’ voices,” she said.",
      "sha256": "563284e4b8f0277c6eb84f78567c1e0da7eeab42c02818536aae02a7cb165403"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "71d5bca0021a82583aa496eb",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "29",
      "locator": "paragraph 29",
      "text": "In January, all three commissioners voted to approve the expansion project, despite many residents speaking out against it. However, the future of the plan is now up in the air, as the commissioners chose to reexamine the project because of the effects the coronavirus pandemic is having on the jail’s space and operations.",
      "sha256": "2194885be6155737eb1939a6af5009d388eeaf35ce0bd83211a86981389b7750"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "6258d4cf5922459e5ce589cf",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "30",
      "locator": "paragraph 30",
      "text": "Regardless, Reid said she has experience with criminal justice she believes would be helpful to further discussions on the project.",
      "sha256": "0a1104a0bdb0878105d156f41149d857ae0e5fc2fdec974348b4ead408c501cb"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "a0c16319b0e0799bf9beace4",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "31",
      "locator": "paragraph 31",
      "text": "Reid works for the Willow Domestic Violence Center, where she serves as the coordinator for the organization’s court advocacy program. In that role, Reid helps survivors of abuse navigate the legal system, which has helped her understand what barriers people face and what contributes to them being put in jail.",
      "sha256": "1e6107fff28e32e02662d7373b4d891357b1aeb8fd38be4b0df42853ce840a6d"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "bf88d765c2a642b1e5b3d9be",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "32",
      "locator": "paragraph 32",
      "text": "Using that knowledge, she said she would like to put the county’s funding and efforts toward social services — such as behavioral health treatment and recovery — which may help decrease the amount of people who are being put in jail and render the project unnecessary.",
      "sha256": "3e77635c3f95d6633b3cda8aa38888df12d96231c5a69f045720da7ac620f1dc"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "abf40a5b6f38f255c64432ec",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "33",
      "locator": "paragraph 33",
      "text": "“I feel, as a county, we haven’t done much to address some of the solutions because the community has had to spend so much time and energy pushing back on this one issue,” Reid said. “Prevention is where our money should be spent.”",
      "sha256": "fb0f3434fc93213402390df6306b31b96cb147621b629fe5c743ba35864716d5"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "ca53d83e4f30230d66f0150d",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "34",
      "locator": "paragraph 34",
      "text": "The pandemic is also having an effect on the county’s revenue streams. While the county does not yet know the full extent of the issue, it is preparing to see a decrease in tax revenues because of an economic downturn associated with the pandemic.",
      "sha256": "ff4e2bb2e0f5c24f2a4e6b5009e21fd32920e56471ddb90b86640a43efdee39b"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "6cc574ad5b2cda308a9dccc2",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "35",
      "locator": "paragraph 35",
      "text": "Reid said she still has a lot to learn about dealing with the financial end of the county’s responsibilities. However, she said the pandemic requires the county’s leadership to refocus the funds the county does have.",
      "sha256": "1814adf7800a560bf6a7e801065e9a687425d82943bce38959a4607f8921a9e5"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "86f24de7fcc0a9ff10db7da4",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "36",
      "locator": "paragraph 36",
      "text": "“There needs to be an immediate refocus of funds and looking at things, like the jail expansion project, and realize that money should be immediately shifted to other resources,” she said.",
      "sha256": "600a2bc50fe1aaf16e9f67a7d84fea7730c55b6abbe02b0df337b09664ac207d"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "117276d220ebd967b0ce5b27",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "37",
      "locator": "paragraph 37",
      "text": "One area Reid said she would like to further invest into is affordable housing, which she said could also serve as a preventive measure to decrease the inmate population at the jail.",
      "sha256": "edf3cba6d473ed1fb554af2221e7e5447b2a92ad173d5d318a831efe68a3487b"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "a3f36614c566ed4ee098cba7",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "38",
      "locator": "paragraph 38",
      "text": "As for rural land use, a common issue for the commissioners, Reid said she’s looking to hear from rural landowners to understand their perspective. She said she doesn’t have personal experience dealing with rural land use, but she thinks the commissioners should consider examining many areas, including environmental impact, before allowing new development.",
      "sha256": "9ddc48d0c64263aec2842f8e23e038df5266fd1e17220008f43e934f2f425b65"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "2dbda6bc3ce7670c7c86a835",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "39",
      "locator": "paragraph 39",
      "text": "Prior to her current position, Reid worked for other nonprofit organizations in New York City and Lawrence, including the United Way of Douglas County.",
      "sha256": "d3294e7bfd62c7bef36eee7152a7e9ed51409245cf86ac7582162a269d31cddc"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "59648abebf167bd2c3adb1c4",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "40",
      "locator": "paragraph 40",
      "text": "She has spent most of her life in Lawrence, graduating from Lawrence High School in 2003. She currently lives in Lawrence’s Prairie Park neighborhood with her partner, Bobbi Henson.",
      "sha256": "a69ef6789ea3f41122bcfada61423f6cfe7fe1681196da3d17a5de7a678314c5"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "782940747de09687fe638a7d",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "41",
      "locator": "paragraph 41",
      "text": "Show/Post Comments",
      "sha256": "82cbf79db40d674e9120a66e9b1c83d66daa02f8c26ab93dfac22046288b93a0"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "89ea666e81f8099490c0ca2a",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "42",
      "locator": "paragraph 42",
      "text": "County Government",
      "sha256": "6643ee5f05f7f83aa37ad58fc94552b6ee6636f88e894125eb9d76f43c051c92"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "a9d49eda04e84a1f7f75f8ff",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "43",
      "locator": "paragraph 43",
      "text": "As budget season winds down, two of Douglas County’s cities have reduced property tax rates, two have increased them",
      "sha256": "5e12687b94b3739de665f08ab8ee99c20b8fd2d73fb8f976fdcb5c767f4e7545"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "68c9a107debacb5a12474243",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "44",
      "locator": "paragraph 44",
      "text": "Douglas County commissioners signal support for beginning a ‘phased approach’ of changes to the county’s zoning code",
      "sha256": "a065b330f3f358cca2fb7ea06b43db6ce9a5ec1abef42da5a9045d6fe2e512ae"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "4fbffa0c871dc03b37863589",
      "document_id": "ks20-reid",
